      "minimumTimeMinutes": 45,
      "body": "# Digital Marketing Ecosystem, Funnels & Customer Journey Mapping\n\nModern digital marketing is an integrated, multi-touchpoint discipline combining creative storytelling, behavioral psychology, data analytics, and performance automation across paid, earned, and owned channels.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Marketing Ecosystem: Paid, Earned, Owned Media (POEM)\n\n```\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                              THE P.O.E.M. FRAMEWORK                             |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 1. PAID MEDIA     | Media you pay for: Google Search Ads, Meta Ads, TikTok Ads,     |\n|                   | Sponsored Content, Display, Influencer collaborations.          |\n|                   | Benefit: Instant traffic, predictable scaling.                  |\n|                   | Downside: Traffic halts the second you turn off budget.         |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 2. OWNED MEDIA    | Channels you control: Company Website, Blog, Email List, SMS,   |\n|                   | Mobile Apps, YouTube Channel, Community Forums.                 |\n|                   | Benefit: Highest margin, durable customer relationships.        |\n|                   | Downside: Requires long-term consistency to build.              |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 3. EARNED MEDIA   | Organic publicity you earn: Press mentions, viral shares,       |\n|                   | organic SEO rankings, word-of-mouth reviews, podcasts.          |\n|                   | Benefit: Highest trust, authoritative brand credibility.        |\n|                   | Downside: Hard to predict, cannot be forced directly.           |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Customer Journey: AIDA vs. Flywheel vs. Funnel Stages\n\nThe traditional marketing funnel maps customer intent progression:\n\n```\n                    [ TOP OF THE FUNNEL (TOFU): AWARENESS ]\n                    - Problem recognition, educational blog posts, social video\n                    - Metric: Impressions, Reach, CTR, Video Completion Rate\n                                       |\n                                       v\n                 [ MIDDLE OF THE FUNNEL (MOFU): CONSIDERATION ]\n                 - Solution comparison, webinars, product demo guides, whitepapers\n                 - Metric: Lead capture, Email opt-ins, MQLs (Marketing Qualified Leads)\n                                       |\n                                       v\n                 [ BOTTOM OF THE FUNNEL (BOFU): CONVERSION ]\n                 - Purchasing decision, free trials, promo codes, direct checkout\n                 - Metric: Conversion Rate (CVR), Sales, SQLs, Customer Acquisitions\n                                       |\n                                       v\n                  [ POST-PURCHASE: RETENTION, ADVOCACY & LOYALTY ]\n                  - Onboarding emails, referral programs, recurring subscriptions\n                  - Metric: Repeat Purchase Rate, Net Promoter Score (NPS), Churn\n```\n\n### The Flywheel Shift:\nWhile a funnel treats customers as an output, the **Flywheel model** treats delighted customers as the input fuel driving momentum through word-of-mouth referrals, organic virality, and compounding repeat revenue.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Financial Unit Economics of Performance Marketing\n\nElite digital marketers evaluate campaigns using financial unit economics rather than vanity vanity metrics:\n\n| Metric | Formula | Benchmark Target | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **CAC** (Customer Acquisition Cost) | `Total Marketing & Sales Spend / Total New Customers Acquired` | Low as possible | Total fully loaded cost to secure one paying customer. |\n| **LTV** (Customer Lifetime Value) | `Average Order Value × Purchase Frequency × Customer Lifespan` | High as possible | Total gross profit generated by a customer over their entire lifecycle. |\n| **LTV:CAC Ratio** | `LTV / CAC` | **3:1 to 5:1** | Ratio < 1:1 loses money on every customer. Ratio > 5:1 means under-investing in growth. |\n| **CAC Payback Period** | `CAC / (Average Monthly Revenue per Customer × Gross Margin %)` | **< 12 Months** | Months required for a customer's gross margin to pay back their acquisition cost. |\n| **ROAS** (Return on Ad Spend) | `Revenue Generated from Ads / Total Ad Spend` | **> 3.0x to 4.0x** | Immediate cash efficiency of paid advertising channels. |\n\n<div class=\"video-container\" style=\"position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; margin: 2rem 0;\">\n  <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/5a4G0kZ04rA\" title=\"Digital Marketing Landscape & Unit Economics\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;\"></iframe>\n</div>"
