      "contentType": "Rich Text",
      "durationMinutes": 75,
      "minimumTimeMinutes": 45,
      "body": "# Technical SEO, Core Web Vitals & Site Performance\n\nTechnical SEO focuses on server configuration, code efficiency, page load speed, and crawlability. Google explicitly uses page speed and user experience metrics as ranking factors in search algorithms.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Web Vitals (CWV) Framework\n\nCore Web Vitals are Google's standardized metrics measuring real-world user page experience:\n\n```\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                             CORE WEB VITALS METRICS                             |\n+-------------------+---------------------+---------------------------------------+\n| METRIC            | TARGET THRESHOLD    | WHAT IT MEASURES                      |\n+-------------------+---------------------+---------------------------------------+\n| 1. LCP            | <= 2.5 seconds      | Largest Contentful Paint: Measures    |\n|                   |                     | perceived loading speed (time taken   |\n|                   |                     | for largest image/text block to render)|\n+-------------------+---------------------+---------------------------------------+\n| 2. INP            | <= 200 milliseconds | Interaction to Next Paint (Replaced   |\n|                   |                     | FID): Measures overall responsiveness |\n|                   |                     | to clicks/keyboard interactions.      |\n+-------------------+---------------------+---------------------------------------+\n| 3. CLS            | <= 0.1 score        | Cumulative Layout Shift: Measures     |\n|                   |                     | visual stability (prevents content    |\n|                   |                     | from jumping around as ads/images load)|\n+-------------------+---------------------+---------------------------------------+\n| 4. TTFB           | <= 800 milliseconds | Time to First Byte: Server response   |\n| (Supporting)      |                     | and network connection latency.       |\n+-------------------+---------------------+---------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Optimizing LCP, INP, and CLS\n\n### How to Fix Poor LCP (> 2.5s):\n- Compress hero banner images using modern formats (**WebP / AVIF**).\n- Use `<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"hero.webp\">` to fetch above-the-fold assets early.\n- Implement Content Delivery Networks (**CDNs** like Cloudflare or Fastly) to serve assets from edge caches nearest to the user.\n\n### How to Fix Layout Shifts (CLS > 0.1):\n- Always specify explicit `width` and `height` attributes on `<img>` and `<iframe>` elements so the browser reserves layout space before download completes:\n  ```html\n  <img src=\"banner.webp\" width=\"1200\" height=\"630\" alt=\"Course Overview\" />\n  ```\n- Reserve fixed CSS min-height containers for dynamically injected third-party display ads.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Crawl Budget Management\n\n**Crawl Budget** is the number of URLs Googlebot can and wants to crawl on your site within a given time period:\n- **Server Response Latency:** If your server responds in 100ms, Googlebot crawls significantly more pages per day than if TTFB is 2,000ms.\n- **Faceted Navigation Waste:** Filtered product lists (e.g., `?sort=price_asc&filter=red`) create millions of duplicate URLs that exhaust crawl budget if not blocked via robots.txt or canonical tags.\n- **404 and Redirect Chains:** Fix 301 redirect chains (`Page A -> Page B -> Page C`) to a single direct 301 hop to preserve crawl bandwidth.\n\n<div class=\"video-container\" style=\"position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; margin: 2rem 0;\">\n  <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/5a4G0kZ04rA\" title=\"Technical SEO & Core Web Vitals\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;\"></iframe>\n</div>"
